---
import Legal from "../../../layouts/Legal.astro";
import { t } from "../../../i18n/sprachen";
const w = t("en");
const schluss = `${w.anmeldeschluss} ${w.jahr}`;
---
<Legal lang="en" seite="teilnahme" title="Participation conditions" kicker="Participation" h1={`Participation conditions`} sub="What applies on the day. Access, schedule, food, conduct and safety.">
<section>
<h2>1 · Principle</h2>
<p>These conditions supplement the <a href="/en/terms">terms and conditions</a>. They govern conduct at the event itself.</p>
<p>By entering, the participant accepts these conditions and the instructions of the staff.</p>
</section>

<section>
<h2>2 · Access</h2>
<p>Access applies only with a valid booking and from the age of 18. The booking is checked at the welcome desk at the cellar.</p>
<p>The meeting point is the Fernand Cina cellar at Bahnhofstrasse 27 in Salgesch, at 10:00. Anyone arriving later calls us.</p>
<p>There is no claim to missed courses or wines.</p>
</section>

<section>
<h2>3 · Schedule and times</h2>
<dl class="def">
<div><dt>10:00</dt><dd>Welcome at the cellar, first wine, music from the first glass</dd></div>
<div><dt>from 10:30</dt><dd>Shuttle or walk to the Clos du Cornalin</dd></div>
<div><dt>11:15</dt><dd>First course</dd></div>
<div><dt>until 14:00</dt><dd>Six courses, guided</dd></div>
<div><dt>from 14:00</dt><dd>Bar and fuller music, drinks billed separately</dd></div>
<div><dt>18:00</dt><dd>End</dd></div>
</dl>
<p>The times are guide values. Shifts in the schedule are possible.</p>
</section>

<section>
<h2>4 · The way to the Clos du Cornalin</h2>
<p>The shuttle leaves the cellar from 10:30. The last return is at 18:00.</p>
<p>The footpath leads through the vineyards and climbs. It is walked at your own responsibility. Sturdy shoes are necessary.</p>
<p>For travel to Salgesch we recommend the train. Seven wines are served across the day.</p>
</section>

<section>
<h2>5 · Food</h2>
<p>The courses are handed out at staffed stations. There is no self-service buffet.</p>
<p>The version chosen at booking applies to all courses. A change on site is excluded.</p>
<h3>5.1 Allergies and intolerances</h3>
<p>Allergies and intolerances are to be reported by {schluss} at the latest, as a reply to the confirmation mail. The kitchen takes them into account where possible.</p>
<p>The kitchen cannot guarantee complete freedom from traces of individual ingredients. In the case of severe allergies, the decision to take part rests with the person concerned.</p>
<h3>5.2 Raw ingredients</h3>
<p>One course contains raw meat. People with a weakened immune system, pregnant women and children usually avoid it. The vegetarian version offers an alternative.</p>
</section>

<section>
<h2>6 · Alcohol and responsibility</h2>
<p>Serving wine is part of the event and runs over several hours. Water is available throughout.</p>
<p>Everyone decides on their own consumption. The staff may stop serving at any time.</p>
<p>Anyone who came by car plans the return accordingly. The organiser takes no responsibility for this.</p>
</section>

<section>
<h2>7 · Weather and equipment</h2>
<p>The event takes place in any weather and partly runs outdoors.</p>
<p>We recommend shoes that allow longer standing and walking, plus a jacket for the evening.</p>
<p>The event is built as a standing format. Seats are available, no personal seat is assigned.</p>
</section>

<section>
<h2>8 · Conduct and house rules</h2>
<p>The Clos du Cornalin is a working vineyard. The vines, the walls and the installations are to be treated with care.</p>
<p>The organiser exercises the house rules. It may send people away in the case of:</p>
<ul>
<li>endangering other guests or the staff</li>
<li>damage to vines, installations or material</li>
<li>substantial disturbance of the event</li>
<li>disregard of instructions</li>
</ul>
<p>No refund is made in these cases.</p>
</section>

<section>
<h2>9 · Animals, luggage, valuables</h2>
<p>Dogs and other animals stay at home.</p>
<p>The participant is responsible for items brought along. There is no supervised cloakroom.</p>
</section>

<section>
<h2>10 · Accessibility</h2>
<p>Access to the Clos du Cornalin runs over natural paths and gravel. It is little suited to wheelchairs and prams.</p>
<p>If your mobility is limited, write to us before booking. We look at what is possible.</p>
</section>

<section>
<h2>11 · Emergency</h2>
<p>In an emergency, turn to the service team on site.</p>
<dl class="def">
<div><dt>Ambulance</dt><dd>144</dd></div>
<div><dt>Police</dt><dd>117</dd></div>
<div><dt>Fire brigade</dt><dd>118</dd></div>
<div><dt>Rega</dt><dd>1414</dd></div>
<div><dt>Emergency Europe</dt><dd>112</dd></div>
</dl>
</section>

<section>
<h2>12 · Recordings</h2>
<p>Photos and films are made at the event for the organiser’s communication. Anyone who does not agree reports this at the welcome desk.</p>
</section>
</Legal>
